description:
CONFIRMED progressive/two-tier discovery and readiness defect: frankensearch default discovery looks only for vector.fast.idx/vector.idx (+ vector.quality.idx), while CASS publishes embedder-named monolithic and sharded FSVI artifacts. The ordinary exact CASS writer and reader already agree on index-<embedder>.fsvi, so this is not a general exact-semantic filename failure. It prevents genuine progressive/quality discovery, obscures ANN/tier bindings, and silently collapses intended two-tier retrieval to exact single-tier fallback.

FRANKENSEARCH SCOPE:
1. Add public `TwoTierIndexPaths` and `TwoTierIndex::open_with_paths` for a required fast FSVI, optional quality FSVI, and optional per-tier ANN sidecars. Explicit mode performs zero filename discovery, copying, or renaming. Default `open(dir)` preserves conventional behavior and missing discovery reports every candidate path.
2. Freeze relative paths to absolute at construction/cache-open so later CWD changes cannot retarget reloads. Retain exact open specification across `IndexCache::reload`; document that `replace` does not rebind it.
3. Every configured role must be a distinct filesystem artifact. Reject lexical equality, existing-file identity/hardlinks, final symlinks, symlinked-ancestor+parent-component aliases, and case-fold aliases on case-insensitive targets before any writable ANN action. For missing leaves, resolve the original OS path semantics through the deepest existing parent; never lexically erase `..` before symlink resolution.
4. ANN sidecar paths are writable. Require trusted stable artifact directories, revalidate the complete role set immediately before every save/re-save, publish atomically, and preserve FSVI bytes on every rejection/failure. If stronger no-follow directory-handle publication is later needed for hostile directories, track it separately rather than overclaiming.
5. Expose read-only actual artifact paths and fast/quality identity metadata needed by the strict vector-space contract bd-jbfg. Reexport the path contract through the facade and update every exhaustive SearchError mapping.
6. This bead does not claim CASS end-to-end repair. Consumer manifest/readiness/writer/query reconciliation is a separate CASS bead and must pin this exact frankensearch commit.

TESTS:
- default preferred/fallback/missing-candidate diagnostics;
- custom fast-only and fast+quality embedder-named paths with search/save/reopen and proof no conventional copies appear;
- missing explicit fast/quality exact path errors;
- cache update/reload with exact retained paths and isolated CWD-change child process;
- role alias matrix, hardlink/symlink/symlinked-ancestor+`..`, missing leaves, platform case behavior; FSVI bytes asserted unchanged;
- custom ANN build/load/rebuild/persistence failure and immediate pre-save revalidation;
- downstream error code/advice/stream/ops mappings;
- generic facade integration plus separate real CASS fresh-process E2E.

