description:
Implement score normalization utilities used throughout the fusion pipeline. Different search sources produce scores on different scales (BM25 scores vs cosine similarity), so normalization is required before combining them.

pub fn min_max_normalize(scores: &mut [f32]) {
    let min = scores.iter().copied().fold(f32::INFINITY, f32::min);
    let max = scores.iter().copied().fold(f32::NEG_INFINITY, f32::max);
    let range = max - min;

    if range.abs() < f32::EPSILON {
        // All scores equal → set to 1.0 (not 0.0, to avoid suppressing results)
        for s in scores.iter_mut() { *s = 1.0; }
        return;
    }

    for s in scores.iter_mut() {
        *s = (*s - min) / range;
    }
}

pub fn normalize_scores(scores: &[f32]) -> Vec<f32> {
    let mut result = scores.to_vec();
    min_max_normalize(&mut result);
    result
}

Also provide z-score normalization as an alternative:
pub fn z_score_normalize(scores: &mut [f32]) { ... }

These are used in:
1. Two-tier blending (normalize fast + quality scores to [0,1] before weighted combination)
2. RRF doesn't need normalization (rank-based, inherently normalized)
3. Reranker score normalization (cross-encoder scores can be arbitrary scale)

