description:
Implement Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) for combining lexical and semantic search results. RRF is the standard fusion algorithm used across all 3 codebases and is well-established in IR literature.

Algorithm:
  score(doc) = Σ 1/(K + rank_i + 1)   for each source i where doc appears
  K = 60 (empirically optimal constant from literature)

pub struct RrfConfig {
    /// RRF constant K (default: 60.0). Higher = more weight to high-ranked docs.
    pub k: f64,
    /// Tie-breaking epsilon (default: 1e-9).
    pub epsilon: f64,
}

pub fn rrf_fuse(
    lexical: &[LexicalHit],
    semantic: &[VectorHit],
    limit: usize,
    offset: usize,
    config: &RrfConfig,
) -> Vec<FusedHit> {
    // 1. Build HashMap<doc_id, FusedHit>
    // 2. For each lexical result (rank 0, 1, ...):
    //    score += 1.0 / (K + rank + 1)
    //    Record lexical_rank, lexical_score
    // 3. For each semantic result (rank 0, 1, ...):
    //    score += 1.0 / (K + rank + 1)
    //    Record semantic_rank, semantic_score
    // 4. Sort by: rrf_score (desc) → in_both_sources (tiebreak) → doc_id (stable)
    // 5. Apply offset and limit
}

Candidate budget (from xf src/hybrid.rs):
pub const CANDIDATE_MULTIPLIER: usize = 3;  // Fetch 3x limit from each source

pub fn candidate_count(limit: usize, offset: usize) -> usize {
    limit.saturating_add(offset).saturating_mul(CANDIDATE_MULTIPLIER)
}

This is the heart of hybrid search — it rewards documents that appear in BOTH lexical and semantic results (they get scores from both sources), which typically produces better results than either source alone.

Environment variable: FRANKENSEARCH_RRF_K (override K constant)

