  - crossbeam::channel::bounded(capacity) for dispatch
  - Manual backpressure: if pending >= threshold, drop and log
  - AtomicU64 for queue depth metrics
  - AIMD rate control implemented manually

AFTER (asupersync):
  - asupersync::channel::mpsc::channel(capacity) — bounded, two-phase
  - Backpressure via channel back-pressure (bounded capacity blocks sender)
  - asupersync::combinator::rate_limit for AIMD-style throttling
  - asupersync::combinator::bulkhead for concurrency isolation
  - Cancel-safe: reserve/commit prevents data loss on cancellation

REVISED ARCHITECTURE:

pub struct EmbeddingJobQueue {
    sender: asupersync::channel::mpsc::Sender<EmbeddingJob>,
    receiver: asupersync::channel::mpsc::Receiver<EmbeddingJob>,
    rate_limiter: asupersync::combinator::RateLimiter,
    metrics: QueueMetrics,
}

impl EmbeddingJobQueue {
    pub fn new(capacity: usize) -> Self {
        let (sender, receiver) = asupersync::channel::mpsc::channel(capacity);
        Self {
            sender,
            receiver,
            rate_limiter: RateLimiter::new(RateLimitPolicy::token_bucket(100, Duration::from_secs(1))),
            metrics: QueueMetrics::default(),
        }
    }

    /// Enqueue a job (cancel-safe, two-phase).
    /// Returns Err if queue is full (backpressure) or cancelled.
    pub async fn enqueue(&self, cx: &Cx, job: EmbeddingJob) -> asupersync::Result<()> {
        // Rate limiting (AIMD-style via token bucket)
        self.rate_limiter.acquire(cx).await?;

        // Two-phase send: reserve slot, then commit
        let permit = self.sender.reserve(cx).await?;  // Blocks if at capacity
        permit.send(job);  // Linear, infallible — no data loss possible
        self.metrics.enqueued.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Drain up to batch_size jobs (non-blocking).
    pub fn drain_batch(&self, cx: &Cx, batch_size: usize) -> Vec<EmbeddingJob> {
        let mut batch = Vec::with_capacity(batch_size);
        for _ in 0..batch_size {
            match self.receiver.try_recv() {
                Ok(job) => batch.push(job),
                Err(_) => break,
            }
        }
        batch
    }
}

BACKPRESSURE MODEL (replaces manual AIMD):
  - Primary: bounded channel capacity (blocks sender when full)
  - Secondary: RateLimiter with token bucket (smooths burst traffic)
  - Tertiary: Budget enforcement on the region (deadline-based drop)
  - On exhaustion: sender.reserve() returns Cancelled or ChannelFull error

EXPECTED-LOSS DROP POLICY (from alien-artifact comment):
  - When channel is full and budget is exhausted:
    Actions: {enqueue, drop_oldest, drop_newest, expand_buffer}
    Loss: drop_oldest loses stale work (loss 2); drop_newest loses fresh work (loss 5); expand_buffer risks OOM (loss 10)
    Decision: drop_oldest (FIFO semantics preserved)
  - This maps naturally to asupersync's bounded channel: oldest items are consumed first

OBLIGATION TRACKING:
  - Every SendPermit is a linear obligation
  - Must be sent() or abort()ed — cannot be silently dropped
  - Lab runtime's ObligationLeakOracle catches leaks automatically

