description:
Add structured tracing and logging throughout the entire frankensearch pipeline using the tracing crate. This is critical for debugging, performance monitoring, and the detailed logging the e2e test scripts need.

Tracing configuration:

1. Crate-level subscriber setup (optional, consumer can bring their own):
   pub fn init_default_tracing(level: tracing::Level) {
       tracing_subscriber::fmt()
           .with_env_filter(EnvFilter::from_default_env()
               .add_directive(format!("frankensearch={}", level).parse().unwrap()))
           .with_timer(tracing_subscriber::fmt::time::uptime())
           .with_target(true)
           .with_thread_ids(true)
           .init();
   }

2. Instrument key operations with spans:

   Embedding:
   #[tracing::instrument(skip(text), fields(model = %self.id(), dim = self.dimension(), text_len = text.len()))]
   fn embed(&self, text: &str) -> SearchResult<Vec<f32>>

   Vector search:
   #[tracing::instrument(skip(index, query), fields(index_size = index.record_count(), dim = index.dimension(), k))]
   fn search_top_k(...)

   RRF fusion:
   #[tracing::instrument(skip(lexical, semantic), fields(lexical_count = lexical.len(), semantic_count = semantic.len(), k = config.k))]
   fn rrf_fuse(...)

   Two-tier search (the big one):
   #[tracing::instrument(skip(self), fields(query_len = query.len(), k, mode))]
   fn search(&self, query: &str, k: usize) -> TwoTierSearchIter

3. Key events to log:

   INFO level:
   - "index_opened" { path, record_count, dimension, embedder_id, format_version }
   - "model_loaded" { model_name, dimension, load_time_ms, category }
   - "search_completed" { phase, result_count, latency_ms, query_len }
   - "index_rebuilt" { old_count, new_count, rebuild_time_ms }

   DEBUG level:
   - "query_embedded" { model, dimension, latency_us }
   - "vector_search_done" { candidates_scanned, results_returned, latency_ms }
   - "rrf_fused" { lexical_candidates, semantic_candidates, fused_count, overlap_count }
   - "scores_blended" { fast_count, quality_count, blend_factor, rank_correlation }
   - "rerank_done" { model, candidates_in, latency_ms, score_range }

   WARN level:
   - "quality_model_unavailable" { reason, fallback }
   - "refinement_timeout" { budget_ms, elapsed_ms }
   - "backpressure_triggered" { queue_depth, threshold }

   TRACE level (very hot path, disabled by default):
   - Individual dot product scores
   - Per-record filter decisions
   - Token-level embedding details

4. Performance timing via tracing spans:
   Every span automatically gets duration. In tests, use tracing-test crate to capture and assert on logged events.

Dependencies:
- tracing = "0.1"
- tracing-subscriber = "0.3" (with fmt, env-filter features)
- tracing-test = "0.2" (dev-dependency, for test assertions on logs)

