description:
Define the Reranker trait in frankensearch-core. Cross-encoder rerankers are used as a second pass after initial retrieval to improve relevance ordering. Must be object-safe.

pub trait Reranker: Send + Sync {
    /// Score query-document pairs. Returns relevance scores (higher = more relevant).
    /// The returned Vec must have the same length as documents.
    fn rerank(&self, query: &str, documents: &[&str]) -> SearchResult<Vec<f32>>;

    /// Model name identifier.
    fn model_name(&self) -> &str;

    /// Maximum input sequence length in tokens.
    fn max_length(&self) -> usize;

    /// Whether this reranker is currently available (model loaded).
    fn is_available(&self) -> bool;
}

This is distinct from bi-encoders (Embedder trait) because cross-encoders attend to query+document simultaneously, producing a relevance score rather than a vector.

Reference implementations:
- cass: src/search/reranker.rs (217 lines) - trait with RerankerError variants
- xf: src/reranker.rs - same trait, slightly different error handling
- agent-mail: not yet integrated (planned)

The trait goes in frankensearch-core, implementations in frankensearch-rerank.

