description:
Implement query classification and adaptive candidate budgeting for hybrid search. Different types of queries benefit from different retrieval strategies -- technical identifiers should lean lexical, natural language queries should lean semantic.

From agent-mail hybrid_candidates.rs (1,234 lines):

Query Classification:

pub enum QueryClass {
    /// Empty or whitespace-only query
    Empty,
    /// Technical identifier: "br-123", "thread:abc", mixed alpha+digits
    Identifier,
    /// Short keyword phrase: 1-2 short tokens
    ShortKeyword,
    /// Natural language: 3+ tokens or long average token length
    NaturalLanguage,
}

impl QueryClass {
    pub fn classify(query: &str) -> Self {
        let tokens: Vec<&str> = query.split_whitespace().collect();
        if tokens.is_empty() { return Self::Empty; }

        // Identifier heuristics (from agent-mail):
        // - Starts with known prefix ("br-", "thread:", "bd-")
        // - Contains underscores or slashes
        // - Mixed alpha+digit tokens
        // - All-hyphenated tokens
        let looks_like_id = tokens.iter().any(|t| {
            t.contains('_') || t.contains('/') ||
            (t.contains('-') && t.chars().any(|c| c.is_ascii_digit())) ||
            (t.chars().any(|c| c.is_ascii_alphabetic()) && t.chars().any(|c| c.is_ascii_digit()))
        });
        if looks_like_id { return Self::Identifier; }

        let avg_len = tokens.iter().map(|t| t.len()).sum::<usize>() / tokens.len();
        if tokens.len() <= 2 && avg_len <= 10 { return Self::ShortKeyword; }

        Self::NaturalLanguage
    }
}

Candidate Budget System:

pub struct CandidateConfig {
    /// Base multiplier for lexical candidates (default: 3x)
    pub lexical_multiplier: f32,
    /// Base multiplier for semantic candidates (default: 3x)
    pub semantic_multiplier: f32,
    /// Minimum candidates per source (default: 20)
    pub min_per_source: usize,
    /// Maximum candidates per source (default: 1000)
    pub max_per_source: usize,
    /// Maximum total candidates (default: 2000)
    pub max_combined: usize,
}

Query-class adjustments (from agent-mail):
- Identifier: lex_mult *= 1.5, sem_mult *= 0.5 (lean lexical for exact matches)
- ShortKeyword: lex_mult *= 1.25, sem_mult *= 0.75 (slight lexical preference)
- NaturalLanguage: lex_mult *= 0.9, sem_mult *= 1.35 (lean semantic for meaning)
- Empty: lex_mult *= 1.0, sem_mult = 0.0 (lexical only, no semantic)

pub struct CandidateBudget {
    pub lexical_count: usize,
    pub semantic_count: usize,
    pub combined_limit: usize,
    pub query_class: QueryClass,
}

impl CandidateBudget {
    pub fn derive(
        requested_limit: usize,
        config: &CandidateConfig,
        query: &str,
    ) -> Self {
        let class = QueryClass::classify(query);
        let (lex_adj, sem_adj) = class.multiplier_adjustments();
        let lex = ((requested_limit as f32) * config.lexical_multiplier * lex_adj)
            .ceil() as usize;
        let sem = ((requested_limit as f32) * config.semantic_multiplier * sem_adj)
            .ceil() as usize;
        let lex = lex.clamp(config.min_per_source, config.max_per_source);
        let sem = sem.clamp(config.min_per_source, config.max_per_source);
        CandidateBudget {
            lexical_count: lex,
            semantic_count: sem,
            combined_limit: (lex + sem).min(config.max_combined),
            query_class: class,
        }
    }
}

This replaces the simple CANDIDATE_MULTIPLIER=3 constant in bd-3un.20 (RRF) with a query-aware system that adapts to what the user is searching for.

