REVIEW FIX: Body contains two conflicting schema designs. The canonical schema should be:

CREATE TABLE documents (
  doc_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  title TEXT NOT NULL,
  content BLOB NOT NULL,
  content_hash BLOB NOT NULL,
  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch()),
  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch())
);

CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE documents_fts USING fts5(
  title, content, content='documents', content_rowid='rowid'
);

The second schema variant with separate metadata/content tables is unnecessary complexity for V1. Single-table with FTS5 content sync is simpler and sufficient.

description:
TASK: Implement storage-backed staleness detector integration.

This bridges the FrankenSQLite storage layer (bd-3w1.11) with the IndexCache staleness detection system (bd-3un.41). Instead of relying solely on file timestamps, the staleness detector queries the document metadata database for precise change detection.

INTEGRATION API:

  pub struct StorageBackedStaleness {
      storage: Arc<Storage>,
      config: StalenessConfig,
  }

  pub struct StalenessConfig {
      /// Minimum number of new/changed documents before triggering rebuild
      pub min_change_threshold: usize,       // Default: 10
      /// Maximum age of index before forced rebuild (even if no changes detected)
      pub max_index_age_secs: Option<u64>,   // Default: None (no age limit)
      /// Check model revision changes (embedder update)
      pub check_model_revision: bool,        // Default: true
      /// Check schema version changes
      pub check_schema_version: bool,        // Default: true
  }

  impl StorageBackedStaleness {
      /// Comprehensive staleness check combining all signals
      pub fn check(&self, index_name: &str, current_embedder_rev: Option<&str>, current_schema: Option<&str>) -> SearchResult<StalenessReport>;

      /// Quick check: just count pending embeddings (fast, no full scan)
      pub fn quick_check(&self, embedder_id: &str) -> SearchResult<QuickStalenessCheck>;
  }

  pub struct StalenessReport {
      pub is_stale: bool,
      pub reasons: Vec<StalenessReason>,
      pub confidence: f32,                   // 0.0 to 1.0
      pub recommended_action: RecommendedAction,
      pub stats: StalenessStats,
  }

  pub struct StalenessStats {
      pub total_documents: usize,
      pub indexed_documents: usize,
      pub pending_documents: usize,
      pub failed_documents: usize,
      pub docs_changed_since_build: usize,
      pub index_age: Duration,
      pub last_build_duration: Option<Duration>,
  }

  pub enum RecommendedAction {
      NoAction,                              // Index is fresh
      IncrementalUpdate { doc_count: usize }, // Only embed new/changed docs
      FullRebuild { reason: String },         // Schema change, model update, etc.
  }

QUICK CHECK SQL (O(1)):
  SELECT COUNT(*) as pending FROM embedding_status
  WHERE embedder_id = ?embedder AND status = 'pending';

  This uses the partial index from bd-3w1.2 and is effectively instant.

INTEGRATION WITH IndexCache (bd-3un.41):
  The IndexCache holds OnceLock<Option<VectorIndex>> for each tier.
  The staleness detector is called:
  1. On cache initialization (first access)
  2. Periodically (configurable interval)
  3. After document ingestion (new content triggers check)

  When staleness is detected:
  - IncrementalUpdate: queue the pending documents for embedding, update vector index in-place
  - FullRebuild: clear the cache, rebuild all indices from the document store

  The document store (FrankenSQLite) is the SOURCE OF TRUTH. Vector indices and Tantivy
  indices are derived/cached artifacts that can always be rebuilt from the source.

CONFIDENCE SCORING:
  Confidence reflects how certain we are that rebuilding would improve results:
  - 0.0: Index is perfectly fresh (no changes)
  - 0.3: A few documents changed (< min_threshold)
  - 0.7: Significant content change (> 10% of documents)
  - 0.9: Model revision changed (embeddings are from wrong model version)
  - 1.0: Schema changed or index missing (rebuild is mandatory)

File: frankensearch-storage/src/staleness.rs

