TASK: Update the facade crate re-exports for storage and durability APIs.

Extend the frankensearch facade crate (bd-3un.30) to re-export the new storage and durability public APIs, so consumers can access everything through a single import.

UPDATED RE-EXPORTS:

  // frankensearch/src/lib.rs

  // ... existing re-exports from bd-3un.30 ...

  // Storage (feature-gated)
  #[cfg(feature = "storage")]
  pub use frankensearch_storage::{
      Storage, StorageConfig,
      DocumentRecord, BatchResult,
      PersistentJobQueue, JobQueueConfig, JobQueueMetrics,
      ContentHasher, DeduplicationDecision,
      IndexMetadata, StalenessCheck, StalenessReason,
      StorageBackedJobRunner, IngestResult, IngestAction,
  };

  // FTS5 (feature-gated, requires storage)
  #[cfg(feature = "fts5")]
  pub use frankensearch_storage::{
      Fts5LexicalSearch, Fts5Config, Fts5Tokenizer, Fts5ContentMode,
  };

  // Durability (feature-gated)
  #[cfg(feature = "durability")]
  pub use frankensearch_durability::{
      RepairCodec, RepairCodecConfig, DurabilityMetrics,
      FileProtector, FileProtectorConfig,
      FsviProtector, ProtectionResult, RepairResult,
      VerifyResult, FileHealth,
  };

ERGONOMIC AUTO-CONFIGURATION:

  The TwoTierSearcher::auto() constructor should detect available features:

  impl TwoTierSearcher {
      pub fn auto(data_dir: &Path) -> SearchResult<Self> {
          // If 'storage' feature enabled:
          //   Open FrankenSQLite database at data_dir/frankensearch.db
          //   Use persistent job queue
          //   Use storage-backed staleness detection
          //
          // If 'durability' feature enabled:
          //   Create FileProtector with default config
          //   Verify indices on load
          //   Protect indices after build
          //
          // If 'fts5' feature enabled AND 'lexical' not enabled:
          //   Use FTS5 as the lexical engine
          //
          // If both 'fts5' and 'lexical' enabled:
          //   Use Tantivy as primary, FTS5 as fallback

          // ... auto-detect embedders, build config ...
      }
  }

DOCUMENTATION ADDITIONS:
  The facade crate's doc comments should explain:
  1. Feature flag selection guide (which features for which use case)
  2. Storage: what it provides and when to use it
  3. Durability: what it protects and the overhead cost
  4. FTS5 vs Tantivy: trade-offs and when to use each

