description:
REPRODUCED HARNESS FAILURE: two back-to-back QG-1 runs on the same fixture/profile/worker/revision reported paired A/B medians 8.412 and 0.855, while the second invocation Criterion absolutes implied about 2.67x in Quill’s favor. A/A null intervals spanned roughly 0.096..1.317 and 0.956..12.012 with 140-209% CV. These runs are measurements but are not decision evidence.

DO NOT PATCH A FORMULA BY GUESS. Discriminate the failure classes:
1. Verify both reporting paths time the exact same unit: corpus preparation, analyzer/tokenization, add, commit/visibility, teardown and bytes/docs denominator. Give each timing scope a versioned operation ID. Criterion and paired paths may coexist only when scope differences are explicit.
2. Record raw per-arm timestamps/durations and stable sample/block IDs. Pair only within the same randomized/interleaved block; assert no missing/duplicated/misaligned pair.
3. Estimate the treatment effect on paired log ratios (robust center plus paired seeded bootstrap CI), while also persisting each arm absolute p50/p95/p99/throughput and a clearly labeled ratio-of-arm-medians diagnostic. Do not confuse median-of-ratios with ratio-of-medians.
4. A/A must execute the identical pipeline twice under randomized order. Evaluate null center, CI width, drift/order/carryover and robust dispersion on log scale. Thresholds are fixture/scale-aware and fixed before live runs; null failure invalidates the decision.
5. INVALID DOES NOT MEAN DISAPPEAR: always persist the raw diagnostic run with status `InvalidNull`/`NoDecision`, reason codes, samples and environment. Never emit an Allow/Block performance claim from it. This preserves immediate measurement without polluting ratchets.
6. Gate decisions use absolute+relative values from the same paired blocks, same executable, corpus and worker. The artifact schema makes contradictory summaries structurally detectable.

TESTS:
- synthetic paired samples with known effects, heteroskedastic/high-variance denominators, outliers and drift;
- deliberately misaligned sample IDs must fail closed;
- injected null noise/order/carryover yields InvalidNull and no claim while retaining raw data;
- same seed deterministic bootstrap; two process invocations fall within predeclared tolerance on a stable synthetic workload;
- cross-report scope mismatch is rejected; same-scope absolute and paired summaries satisfy a mathematically justified consistency check;
- randomized order balance and warmup separation tests;
- artifact round-trip/golden schema and severity precedence Fatal > Block > Quarantine > Allow/Provisional.

LOGGING: at debug level emit bounded raw sample records with block ID, engine/order, operation scope/version, docs/bytes, duration, warmup state and timestamps; info table reports absolutes, paired effect/CI, null diagnostics and explicit decision status. Capture machine load/governor/cores at start/end.

Ratios alone hide which engine moved and cannot be sanity-checked against user SLOs. Every QG artifact must carry absolute measurements for BOTH engines from the same paired blocks, the paired relative effect/CI, A/A null diagnostics, and raw bounded samples.

SCHEMA (new version; old artifacts never masquerade as current):
- run/gate/cell ID; decision status including MeasuredProvisional, InvalidNull, Quarantine, Block, Allow; required-versus-diagnostic designation; reason/severity precedence;
- operation scope/version and exact numerator/denominator;
- per engine absolute raw samples and summary: durations/latency p50,p95,p99, docs/s, MB/s, commits/s as applicable; sample/iteration/warmup counts;
- paired block IDs/order, log-ratio effect and seeded bootstrap CI; A/A raw/summaries/validity;
- corpus/query/qrels hashes, sizes, content bytes, generator seed/revision, query class and k;
- executing ELF SHA-256 obtained from the running binary, git tree/revision including dirty-state hash, Cargo.lock/rustc/target/profile/features, thread/heap budgets;
- machine identity, CPU/NUMA/OS, governor, load/start-end, peak RSS method/value, filesystem/storage/cold-cache procedure.

GATE ABSOLUTES include: QG-1 indexing docs/s+MB/s; QG-2 ingest stage breakdown; QG-3 update-to-searchable commit/visibility latency; QG-4 commit p50/p95/p99 over the required durable commit count; QG-5 merge docs/s+MB/s; QG-6 per-query-class p50/p95/p99 and QPS on realistic query sets; QG-7 RSS and bytes/doc on disk; QG-8 scaling by thread count; QG-9 truly cold open ms with cache-state proof; QG-10 dependency/build-size facts outside noisy timing A/A.

INVALID runs are persisted with raw samples and NoDecision, never dropped and never ratcheted as evidence. Human Markdown/CSV tables are derived from the authoritative JSON and must round-trip/reconcile. Cross-check the README baseline envelope; disagreement opens a finding rather than being footnoted.

TESTS: schema rejects missing arm/absolute/null/provenance/raw/scope fields; executing-ELF hash self-test; raw-to-summary recomputation; invalid-null cannot yield claim; old-schema migration is explicit/read-only; human table matches JSON; privacy/redaction canaries; platform-specific RSS/cold-cache probes report unsupported rather than zero.

notes:
ROOT CAUSE FOUND 2026-07-26 (read-only diagnosis; I have NOT edited any file).

crates/frankensearch-quill/src/query.rs:651-662 -- default-field validation HARD-REQUIRES positions:

    if !matches!(
        field.kind,
        FieldKind::Text {
            analyzer: AnalyzerKind::FrankensearchDefault,
            positions: true,            // <-- hard requirement
        }
    ) {
        return Err(QueryParserConfigError::InvalidDefaultField { schema: schema.name, field: name });
    }

The harness's NO_POSITION_FIELDS (benches/perf_matrix.rs:60-67) declares content with positions: false, as a position-free schema must. So the predicate can never be satisfied.

THIS IS NOT MERELY A HARNESS BUG -- IT IS A QUILL CAPABILITY GAP. As written, a position-free Quill index can never have a default field, which means Quill CANNOT PARSE ANY BARE (non-field-qualified) QUERY against a position-free index at all. Position-free indexing is a legitimate, valuable configuration (smaller postings, faster ingest) and plain term queries do not need positions. Only PHRASE queries do.

RECOMMENDED FIX (preserves the capability rather than deleting the fixture):
  1. Relax the default-field predicate to require analyzer == FrankensearchDefault and Text kind, WITHOUT requiring positions: true.
  2. Move the positions requirement to where it actually applies: reject a PHRASE query (and slop/proximity) at parse/lowering time when the target field has positions: false, with a distinct, accurate error such as PhraseRequiresPositions { schema, field } -- not InvalidDefaultField, which misdescribes the problem and is what made this look like a harness misconfiguration.
  3. query.rs:6033 has an existing test asserting the current behaviour; it must be updated deliberately as part of the change, not deleted.

TESTS REQUIRED (beyond those already listed on this bead):
  - Position-free schema + bare term query -> Ok, returns hits.
  - Position-free schema + phrase query -> Err(PhraseRequiresPositions) naming the field, NOT InvalidDefaultField.
  - Position-ful schema + phrase query -> unchanged, still Ok.
  - Differential: the same bare term query returns identical doc ids against position-on and position-off indexes over the same corpus (positions must not change which documents MATCH, only whether phrases can be expressed).

OWNERSHIP: query.rs is in the Quill crate. MossySpire holds index.rs and argus.rs; this is neither. Whoever takes it should reserve crates/frankensearch-quill/src/query.rs first.

