HANDOFF — exact index.rs patch, ready to apply (MossySpire holds index.rs; I am not touching it).

CURRENT (index.rs ~5331-5343, inside validate_query_lowering's Query::Phrase arm, under the terms.len() > 1 guard):

                for field in fields {
                    if !matches!(
                        query_field_kind(schema, field.field_id)?,
                        FieldKind::Text { positions: true, .. }
                    ) {
                        return Err(QuillIndexError::UnsupportedQuery {
                            detail: format!("phrase names non-positioned field {}", field.field_id),
                        });
                    }
                }

MINIMAL REPLACEMENT (one edit, no recursion concern — 'query' at this point IS the Phrase node, so validate_index_capabilities inspects exactly this phrase and does not re-walk children):

                crate::query::validate_index_capabilities(query, schema).map_err(|error| {
                    QuillIndexError::UnsupportedQuery { detail: error.to_string() }
                })?;

That alone upgrades the message from 'phrase names non-positioned field 3' to 'operator phrase requires positions on field content of schema <name>, which is indexed without them' — schema + field NAME + operator, per the bead.

PREFERRED (keeps the type, needs one variant in QuillIndexError, your file):

    #[error(transparent)]
    QueryCapability(#[from] crate::query::QueryCapabilityError),

then the call site is just:
                crate::query::validate_index_capabilities(query, schema)?;

The typed form is what the acceptance criteria ask for ('returns typed PositionsRequired with field/operator'), so callers and the total comparator can match on it instead of parsing a string.

EQUIVALENCE NOTE — the two checks already agree, so this is a precision upgrade, not a behaviour change:
- both exempt a single-term phrase (your terms.len() > 1 guard; my terms.len() < 2 early return),
- both require FieldKind::Text { positions: true, .. } on EVERY field the phrase names,
- both reject on the first offending field.
One deliberate difference: on an unknown field_id mine reports the id as '#<id>' rather than propagating query_field_kind's error, because at that point the field-existence check has already run in the Term/bound paths. If you prefer the existing error precedence, call query_field_kind first and keep the capability call for the positions axis only.

VERIFIED SAFE TO RELAX (I checked before landing the parser change): the ONLY production position dependence in the crate is this phrase guard. snippet.rs references positions nowhere; every other 'positions: true' in quill src is past the mod tests boundary (index.rs:7176). So positionless schemas becoming constructible does not newly expose any other path that assumes position lists.
